    lib_nogc_sync_mut_missing_modules_2026-09-16, 0, "2026-11-28 p3sweep8: root cause - every missing module existed verbatim on the unmerged branch origin/chore/merge-share-history (Aug 27), never landed on release/1.0.0; the specs were written against it. Ported the canonical implementations (server_worker_policy, domain_arena_v2, enterprise_assets/expense/quality/warehouse, io/hal_buffer_dispatch + hal_process_socket_dispatch), extended the HAL C twin for the receipt contract (HAL_ACCESS_*_V3 tokens exist in no reachable commit - honest implementation: fixed-slot table, issue to publish(READY/POISONED) to single-winner consume), restored both selfchecks, and fixed check-hal-runtime-buffer-dispatch-v3.shs to resolve the toolchain-emitted selfcheck(.exe) on Windows. Verification: all 7 affected specs 48/48 PASS; 14 neighbours 8 PASS with the 6 failures reproducing byte-identically at baseline. Residuals: the two sibling HAL check scripts need POSIX hosts (pre-existing). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/lib/nogc_sync_mut/io/hal_buffer_dispatch_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/lib/nogc_sync_mut/enterprise_assets/enterprise_assets_suite_spec.spl"

